# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# plexmaton — local-only Rust workspace
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Third-party reference snapshots -------------------------------------
# Cloned upstream sources live here for study only. They are never vendored,
# committed, or treated as this repo's source. Each child is its own git repo.
.references/

# --- Parallel checkouts ---------------------------------------------------
# Worktrees live inside the repository but are never part of it. `.worktrees/`
# is this project's convention; `.claude/worktrees/` is where one agent harness
# puts them by default, and both are ignored so no tool has to be configured to
# keep the main checkout clean. Without these lines a nested worktree doubles
# every corpus search hit, which is a worse failure than the disk it costs.
/.worktrees/
/.claude/worktrees/

# --- Rust build artifacts -------------------------------------------------
# Cargo's default output directory (and any CARGO_TARGET_DIR under the tree).
/target/
# Common alternative target dirs used by parallel/agent builds.
/target-*/
**/*.rs.bk

# Native artifacts that leak out of build scripts, FFI experiments, or
# cdylib/cbindgen output.
**/*.o
**/*.obj
**/*.rlib
**/*.rmeta
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.dylib
**/*.dll
**/*.a
**/*.lib
**/*.pdb
**/*.d

# --- Cargo.lock policy ----------------------------------------------------
# This is expected to ship a binary, so Cargo.lock SHOULD be committed for
# reproducible builds. If this project ever becomes library-only, uncomment:
# Cargo.lock

# --- Crates.io packaging --------------------------------------------------
*.crate
/package/

# --- Fuzzing (cargo-fuzz) -------------------------------------------------
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/symfog-exports/

# --- Coverage, profiling, sanitizers --------------------------------------
/coverage/
*.profraw
*.profdata
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov
.tarpaulin-cache/
/codecov/
miri/
sanitizer.*

# NOTE: proptest-regressions/ is intentionally NOT ignored. Those files are
# repro seeds and belong in version control.

# --- Benchmarks / local measurement output --------------------------------
/bench-results/
/benches/report/
*.jsonl.bak

# --- Editor / IDE ---------------------------------------------------------
/.idea/
/.vscode/
/.fleet/
/.zed/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# --- OS noise -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# --- Local runtime state, secrets, scratch --------------------------------
# Anything this workspace decides to keep machine-local rather than shared.
/.local/
/.cache/
/.tmp/
/tmp/
/scratch/
*.log
*.pid
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# --- Python / Node sidecars (scripts, tooling) ----------------------------
# Allowed only if helper scripts get added later.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
